  "id": "ENT058",
  "title": "The Spiral Lock That Shows Its Work",
  "family": "fiction",
  "category": "mechanical puzzles",
  "premise": "A keeper must release a toy treasure tray using three concentric rings, but random turns keep hiding the exit slot. A cutaway reveals that every ring needs its notch at the top; the keeper aligns the outer, middle, and inner notches and slides out a single celebratory biscuit.",
  "hook": "The lock is not guessing. We are.",
  "visible_action": "Opaque cover becomes transparent; three notches rotate independently to a top marker; a straight pin lifts; tray slides forward.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "Make the hidden condition visible before trying more moves.",
  "gate": "Invented toy notch puzzle, not a real security-device bypass; production must show a consistent pin path and independent ring motion.",
